      "id": "GCP-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-galois-character-complement",
      "title": "Removing one invariant line leaves the same comparison with one fewer entry",
      "hypotheses": "The first lift is semisimple, contains the transferred line and has dimension at least one. Both lists satisfy cross-list disjointness and the augmented identity holds at every group element.",
      "statement": "A fixed invariant complement loses one dimension, remains semisimple and continuous when the original representation is continuous, and satisfies the shortened identity. Repetition within a list is allowed.",
