    {
      "id": "GCP-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-galois-character-local",
      "title": "The same residual representation preserves prescribed local data at every applicable place",
      "hypotheses": "Fix ℓ and the coefficient embedding. Give the lifted row and its individual character lines at a place with compatible multisets of Frobenius parameters and filtered jumps. For the automorphic application assume the prescribed odd-rank local statements and the two-lift theorem.",
      "statement": "A rank-n continuous semisimple residual representation satisfies every consequent local comparison for that choice of lifts. Twisting back and identifying weakly attached representatives yields a common representation at every permitted split place carrying Satake data.",
